{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1100 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "4aac6ef1be9be39a97711a6014b3c0b421cc125909410d17059cb09874c8836e" :edb/db-before-t 1099 :edb/db-after-t 1100 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534412 50 #inst "2026-10-07T01:24:15.130Z" 13194139534412 true] [17592186059649 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286890 13194139534412 true] [17592186064095 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286883 13194139534412 true] [17592186096763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286903 13194139534412 true] [17592186105778 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286900 13194139534412 true] [17592186115120 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286920 13194139534412 true] [17592186147565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286906 13194139534412 true] [17592186157623 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534412 true] [17592186157623 1100 "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $x^{2} \\cdot 4^{x + 1} + 5x \\cdot 4^{x + 1} + 6 \\cdot 4^{x + 1} = 0$ are$x =$\n{{field-1}} and $x =$\n{{field-2}}.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"solving-an-exponential-equation-by-rearranging-the-equation-and-then-factoring\"></a>" 13194139534412 false] [17592186157623 1100 "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+5x\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+6\\cdot {4}^{x+1}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534412 true] [17592186157623 1145 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+5x\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+6\\cdot {4}^{x+1} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5x+6){4}^{x+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+6=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{4}^{x+1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+5x+6=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x+3)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-3,-2.$\n\n- The equation ${4}^{x+1}=0$ has no solutions because ${4}^{x+1}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-2.\n$$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186171953 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286897 13194139534412 true] [17592186175982 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286913 13194139534412 true] [17592186286883 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286884 13194139534412 true] [17592186286883 1089 "q-113930" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286883 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534412 true] [17592186286883 1100 "$\\int (3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286883 1113 #uuid "50fceeb6-a7d6-58ef-a20c-c22efdfa93b4" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286883 1145 "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+7(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286885 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286886 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286887 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286888 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286889 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1041 "selection" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286888 13194139534412 true] [17592186286884 1110 #uuid "73b21915-4309-58a2-83cf-9cc16a98ba0e" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286885 1034 "10{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286885 1111 #uuid "18bc89ef-0f20-546c-84bc-17d810a50c8b" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286886 1034 "-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286886 1111 #uuid "f6c09a31-c639-5d1b-9297-65142d039d20" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286887 1034 "-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286887 1111 #uuid "dd48664d-d1a9-5f09-9d91-a82bbf3798f5" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286888 1034 "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286888 1111 #uuid "c3e1179d-e34e-5b5d-8d5c-1b78ec75e92c" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286889 1034 "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286889 1111 #uuid "26b29c86-e7c4-586d-af2d-320f75e272d9" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286890 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286891 13194139534412 true] [17592186286890 1089 "q-120733" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286890 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534412 true] [17592186286890 1100 "Let $a=⟨1,-2,0⟩$ and $b=⟨1,-3,-2⟩.$ Find $3a+2b.$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286890 1113 #uuid "37edf627-e377-59ee-8553-a795c51e889f" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286890 1145 "To compute $3a+2b,$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2b & =3\\cdot ⟨1,-2,0⟩+2\\cdot ⟨1,-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,0⟩+⟨2,-6,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-12,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286892 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286893 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286894 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286895 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286896 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1041 "selection" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286896 13194139534412 true] [17592186286891 1110 #uuid "b2129908-e8fc-5fa2-896e-13950725f919" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286892 1034 "⟨3,-5,2⟩" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286892 1111 #uuid "97df4ca6-3f77-57ec-83a8-053ba7dc8769" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286893 1034 "⟨3,-6,0⟩" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286893 1111 #uuid "a48217c1-80f5-5b37-b8bd-b4d0b1b2fdb0" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286894 1034 "⟨5,-11,2⟩" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286894 1111 #uuid "5fa2d796-988a-5969-bfcb-45026acb9122" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286895 1034 "⟨2,-6,-4⟩" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286895 1111 #uuid "dd840db7-c351-5954-bac9-cd7da7fffd95" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286896 1034 "⟨5,-12,-4⟩" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286896 1111 #uuid "0b101fbd-232d-5239-ad56-303bd5239347" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286897 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286898 13194139534412 true] [17592186286897 1089 "q-277246" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286897 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534412 true] [17592186286897 1100 "Find the root of $f(x)=-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286897 1113 #uuid "da4fbcaf-98e0-53a1-a049-ba27867c451c" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286897 1145 "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1 & =0 \\\\ -\\sqrt[9]{9-12x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{9-12x} & =-1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[9]{9-12x})^{9} & =(-1)^{9} \\\\ 9-12x & =-1 \\\\ -12x & =-10 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{5}{6}.$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286899 13194139534412 true] [17592186286898 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534412 true] [17592186286898 1041 "field-1" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286898 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286899 13194139534412 true] [17592186286898 1110 #uuid "1ec32963-41d1-5fbe-bf53-d129c1b4ac67" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286899 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286899 1111 #uuid "b1fde28e-0c4d-5810-8db2-57c2fe530376" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286900 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286901 13194139534412 true] [17592186286900 1089 "q-337034" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286900 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534412 true] [17592186286900 1100 "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{5}-7{x}^{3}+2x-9)=${{field-1}}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286900 1113 #uuid "fcf79804-1447-5e6a-9876-af943cc16ecc" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286900 1145 "We identify the leading term and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{5}-7{x}^{3}+2x-9) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\infty \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286902 13194139534412 true] [17592186286901 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534412 true] [17592186286901 1041 "field-1" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286901 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286902 13194139534412 true] [17592186286901 1110 #uuid "1bf0396c-0208-5828-adaf-759d684902b9" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286902 1034 "\\infty" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286902 1111 #uuid "570adc82-cd21-5619-aec3-f919a02d9043" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286903 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286904 13194139534412 true] [17592186286903 1089 "q-344143" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286903 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534412 true] [17592186286903 1100 "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\frac{{e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{x-2}.$\n\n| ${y}^{′}$ | $=$ | $(${{field-1}}$){e}^{3{x}^{2}}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $(x-2)^{2}$ |" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286903 1113 #uuid "dd90d514-01b1-5378-a6f1-668663ee7966" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286903 1145 "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)={e}^{3{x}^{2}}$ and the denominator $v(x)=x-2.$\n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=6x{e}^{3{x}^{2}},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=1.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x{e}^{3{x}^{2}})(x-2)-({e}^{3{x}^{2}})(1)}{(x-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3{x}^{2}}(6x(x-2)-1)}{(x-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6{x}^{2}-12x-1){e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{(x-2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286904 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286905 13194139534412 true] [17592186286904 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534412 true] [17592186286904 1041 "field-1" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286904 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286905 13194139534412 true] [17592186286904 1110 #uuid "41241f81-f0c3-5c9a-bad2-be42855e0d3a" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286905 1034 "6x^2-12x-1" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286905 1111 #uuid "25c3e58c-2442-5d56-99fb-c0b3cad501c9" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286906 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286907 13194139534412 true] [17592186286906 1089 "q-61900" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286906 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534412 true] [17592186286906 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/assets/93a2ddce7e46f9855f0dd9ea499ae2762cb4538f844ecf7bed7d15d1669b0815.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular prism above if it is $2\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $3\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286906 1113 #uuid "1a826bad-db18-5714-a7b1-b24aaab55937" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286906 1145 "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/assets/66836a9004af1cc947cbcd70d99f696dd41eaca76214ca4f45a4e8434a7ec7f2.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $2\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=2\\times 3=6\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $3\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=3\\times 3=9\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the rectangular prism consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 6+2\\times 9 \\\\  & =24+18 \\\\  & =42\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286908 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286909 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286910 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286911 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286912 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1041 "selection" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286909 13194139534412 true] [17592186286907 1110 #uuid "c63731f0-38d7-5d5c-92d3-e426c953e29f" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286908 1034 "54\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286908 1111 #uuid "e5836484-db81-5bac-9204-7f129f355db2" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286909 1034 "42\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286909 1111 #uuid "cb96bd79-8a0e-511a-9846-d6aff345451f" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286910 1034 "46\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286910 1111 #uuid "d775e4da-bff3-5244-b679-627a622bc381" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286911 1034 "48\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286911 1111 #uuid "e95ab778-0380-58d1-b06d-3d510d9e66ca" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286912 1034 "36\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534412 true] [17592186286912 1111 #uuid "00eb5f51-a676-5747-9833-0c9819c41c5e" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286913 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286914 13194139534412 true] [17592186286913 1089 "q-66671" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286913 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534412 true] [17592186286913 1100 "If $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-3$ for some $x$, then find the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\pi ).$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286913 1113 #uuid "0e64915a-a625-5406-a66c-f53248a7caab" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286913 1145 "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=9$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-3,$ then $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\pi )=-3.$" 13194139534412 true] [17592186286914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286915 131941